{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "כי יקרא קן צפור", :translit "ki yikarei ken tzipor", :gloss "if a bird's nest is encountered"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Derivation of a practical prohibition from the wording of the verse: one should not watch birds mating."}], :frame {:text "The term יקרא (\"is encountered\") is read as an occasion of chance: one happens upon a nest, suggesting the bird was seen in a vulnerable state. From this the prohibition is derived against watching animals or birds mate. See Shabbat 86a and Berakhot 23a for prohibitions of inappropriate gazing and modesty concerns.", :sources ["Shabbat 86a" "Berakhot 23a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "יקרא קן", :translit "yikarei ken", :gloss "is encountered, a nest"} {:he "מזומן", :translit "mezuman", :gloss "prepared / ready"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "יקרא קן", :b "פרט למזומן"}], :frame {:text "The commandment of shiluach ha-ken (sending the mother bird) applies only when one chances upon a nest, not when the nest was prepared in advance. The gematria of יקרא קן equals פרט למזומן (excluding the prepared), reinforcing the word יקרא as 'happened upon.' See Chullin 12a-b for the parameters of the mitzvah.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 22:6" "Chullin 12a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "אפרוחים או ביצים", :translit "efrochim o beitzim", :gloss "chicks or eggs"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "אפרוחים או ביצים", :b "בצריכין לאמן"}], :frame {:text "The verse specifies chicks or eggs that still need the mother bird, meaning they are dependent on her and have not yet become independent. See Chullin 141b for the halakhic requirement that the chicks must be fledglings still dependent on the mother for the mitzvah to apply.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 22:6" "Chullin 141b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Derivation of a practical prohibition from the wording of the verse: one should not watch birds mating.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:a-value 461, :b-value 462, :lens :standard, :equal? false, :kind :gematria, :b "פרט למזומן", :by :selah, :colel? true, :a "יקרא קן"} {:a-value 504, :b-value 503, :lens :standard, :equal? false, :kind :gematria, :b "בצריכין לאמן", :by :selah, :colel? true, :a "אפרוחים או ביצים"}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:38:15.934963513Z", :model "glm-5.2"}